<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	DisplayXR Dashboard.app (src/dashboard, Avalonia / .NET 10), signed with
	the hardened runtime on Developer ID builds.

	allow-jit: CoreCLR compiles managed code at run time into MAP_JIT memory.
	Without it the hardened runtime refuses the mapping and the app dies before
	its first line ("Failed to create CoreCLR, HRESULT: 0x80070008"; measured
	with a hardened-runtime signature).

	No library-validation exception: the app dlopen()s only its own Skia /
	HarfBuzz / AvaloniaNative dylibs from Contents/MacOS, which sign-tree signs
	with the same Developer ID, so their Team ID matches. (The ad-hoc tree of
	an unsigned build has no hardened runtime, so validation does not apply.)
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
